{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"A0A509AKI1","uniProtkbId":"PIMM2_PLABA","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2020-12-02","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2019-09-18","entryVersion":24,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":4.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Plasmodium berghei (strain Anka)","taxonId":5823,"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"Proteomes","id":"UP000074855"}],"lineage":["Eukaryota","Sar","Alveolata","Apicomplexa","Aconoidasida","Haemosporida","Plasmodiidae","Plasmodium","Vinckeia"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Subtilisin-like protease PIMMS2"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q8I0V0"}],"value":"3.4.21.62"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"value":"Midgut invasion ookinete protein 2"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"value":"PIMMS2"},"orfNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"EMBL","id":"VUC56492.1"}],"value":"PBANKA_1106900"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29873127"}],"value":"Probable serine protease which plays a role in ookinete traversal of the mosquito host midgut epithelium"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity for peptide bonds, and a preference for a large uncharged residue in P1. Hydrolyzes peptide amides.","ecNumber":"3.4.21.62","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q8I0V0"}]}},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"value":"It is not clear how the protein localizes at the cell membrane. There is a predicted transmembrane domain encompassing the end of the catalytic domain which appears to be intracellular suggesting a single-pass type II membrane topology"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"value":"Cell membrane","id":"SL-0039"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"value":"Expression is restricted to mosquito host midgut stages (at protein level) (PubMed:28559405). Specifically, expression begins after gametocyte activation and peaks in mature ookinetes (at protein level) (PubMed:28559405). Not expressed in the oocyst (PubMed:28559405)"}],"commentType":"DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29873127"}],"value":"Ookinetes fail to traverse the midgut epithelium resulting in a reduced number of oocysts in the gut epithelium of the mosquito host, A.gambiae or A.stephensi (PubMed:28559405, PubMed:29873127). Gametogenesis, and ookinete development and motility are normal (PubMed:28559405). The capacity to infect the mouse host by the few sporozoites made in the mosquito host is not affected (PubMed:28559405)"}],"commentType":"DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the peptidase S8 family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"value":"The three residues, Asp, His and Ser forming the catalytic triad are conserved (PubMed:28559405). However, the conserved motifs HGT and GTS, which encompass His and Ser residues of subtilases, respectively, are not present in PIMMS2, suggesting that the catalytic triad may be non-functional (PubMed:28559405)"}],"commentType":"CAUTION"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":836,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Subtilisin-like protease PIMMS2","featureId":"PRO_0000451407"},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":802,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":836,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Disordered","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":155,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":155,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Charge relay system","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU10080"}]},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":222,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":222,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Charge relay system","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P00782"}]},{"type":"Active site","location":{"start":{"value":414,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":414,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Charge relay system","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P00782"}]},{"type":"Mutagenesis","location":{"start":{"value":155,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":155,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Reduced number of oocysts in the gut epithelium of the mosquito host; when associated with A-222 and A-414.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"alternativeSequence":{"originalSequence":"D","alternativeSequences":["A"]}},{"type":"Mutagenesis","location":{"start":{"value":222,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":222,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Reduced number of oocysts in the gut epithelium of the mosquito host; when associated with A-155 and A-414.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28559405"}],"alternativeSequence":{"originalSequence":"H","alternativeSequences":["A"]}},{"type":"Mutagenesis","location":{"start":{"value":414,"modif